#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""omarchy-zapret2: the manager behind the Omarchy zapret2 plugin.

Every user command prints one JSON object on stdout (long jobs print JSON
progress lines first). Commands starting with "_" are the privileged half and
refuse to run unless root:

  _install / _uninstall   through pkexec (or sudo), once per install/update
  _run / _stop            ExecStart / ExecStopPost of omarchy-zapret2.service
  _blockcheck             ExecStart of omarchy-zapret2-blockcheck.service
  _hosts                  apply or remove the Flowseal hosts block in /etc/hosts

The units run the root-owned copy in /opt/omarchy-zapret2/app, never the
plugin folder. That copy treats everything under /var/lib/omarchy-zapret2
(written by the user, without a password) as untrusted data: settings are
enums, lists are re-validated line by line, custom strategies pass an
allowlist of nfqws2 options and Lua desync functions.

  status                       JSON state (what the widget reads)
  setup                        download the latest zapret2 release, verify it, install (one prompt)
  engine check                 installed vs latest release
  updates check                background check: engine, lists, presets (cached in status)
  on | off | restart           the bypass service
  set <key> <value>            preset, game (off|tcp|udp|all), ipset (loaded|none|any),
                               voice (compatible|standard|off), ipv6 (on|off), autostart (on|off),
                               update_check (on|off), lang (en|ru), gametcp|gameudp <ports>, discordfake|gamefake <default|blob>
  presets                      built-in and custom strategies
  presets update               fetch fresh Flowseal strategies
  hosts on|off|status          Flowseal hosts block in /etc/hosts
  services | service on|off <name>  per-service host picker (Telegram, WhatsApp, ...)
  discord-cache clear          delete Discord cache folders
  dns status|flush               show DNS servers, flush DNS cache
  custom save <name> | show <name> | rm <name>     own strategies (save reads stdin)
  strategy import [--name <name>] [file|--url-stdin]   import a strategy (stdin text, file, or http(s) link on stdin)
  strategy copy <src> [new-name]               duplicate an own (my-*) strategy
  list show <name> | list save <name> [--no-restart]   user lists (save reads stdin)
  export                           backup settings + user lists + own strategies (base64 zip)
  import [file]                    restore a backup (base64 zip from stdin or file)
  export [--stdout] [--file PATH]  backup settings, own strategies and user lists (zip)
  import [--file PATH]             restore a backup (same validators, stdin is base64)
  lists update                 fetch fresh upstream lists (Flowseal)
  check [domain...]            reachability of YouTube, Discord, Google, Cloudflare (or the domains)
  autopick [p1,p2,...]         try strategies one by one, keep the best
  circular [plan|status|stop]  build a per-domain strategy rotation from preset checks
  blockcheck start [domain...] [--level quick|standard|force] | stop | status | save <index>
  doctor | diagnostics | first-run | logs [n] | desktop on|off | remove [--purge]
"""

